Tenali Rama and the Magic Well (Raw Story)

One day, a man came to King Krishnadevaraya and complained that his neighbor had stolen his money.

The neighbor denied the accusation and said he was innocent.

The king was confused because there was no proof.

He asked Tenali Rama to solve the problem.

Tenali thought for a moment and said, “Bring both men to the well outside the village.”

When they reached the well, Tenali said, “This is a magic well. It knows the truth. Anyone who lies will be punished.”

Both men looked nervous.

Tenali then asked each man to drop a coin into the well and tell the truth.

The innocent man stepped forward confidently and dropped his coin.

The guilty man hesitated. He was scared of being caught.

Tenali noticed his fear and said, “Your Majesty, this man is the thief.”

The king asked, “How can you be sure?”

Tenali replied, “An honest person is never afraid of the truth, but a guilty person always is.”

The guilty man hung his head and confessed.

The king praised Tenali Rama for his wisdom and punished the thief.

💖 Moral:

A guilty mind is always afraid.